invariant: INV-74
file: src/tcp_seal.c
catches: tcp_nonblocking_loop_test
reason: ch_seal_in_place seals from the last record to the first without
  setting each record's sequence number, so the last record takes the
  first number and the peer, which opens the records in the order they go
  out, finds a tag that does not match on the first record of every write
  of two records or more (RFC 9846 §5.3).

--- old
        t->wr.seq = first + i;
        size_t out_len = 0;
--- new
        size_t out_len = 0;
